    "377f5fde-6fe5-4af1-8009-262d7c5dcf45": {
      "id": "377f5fde-6fe5-4af1-8009-262d7c5dcf45",
      "message": {
        "id": "377f5fde-6fe5-4af1-8009-262d7c5dcf45",
        "author": {
          "role": "assistant",
          "name": null,
          "metadata": {}
        },
        "create_time": 1770939515.450939,
        "update_time": null,
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "A mini WiFi camera **does NOT always need to be on the same network** — it depends on how you're trying to use it.\n\nHere are the two main situations:\n\n---\n\n### ✅ 1. Viewing Through the Manufacturer’s App (Cloud-Based Cameras)\nMost modern mini WiFi cameras (like ones from brands such as entity[\"company\",\"TP-Link\",\"networking company\"], entity[\"company\",\"EZVIZ\",\"smart camera brand\"], or entity[\"company\",\"Wyze\",\"smart home company\"]) work like this:\n\n- The camera connects to your home WiFi.\n- The camera streams video to the company’s cloud server.\n- You log into the app from anywhere.\n- As long as **both the camera and your phone have internet access**, you can view live video.\n\n👉 In this case, you do **NOT** need to be on the same WiFi network.\n\n---\n\n### ⚙️ 2. Direct / Local Network Cameras (No Cloud)\nSome cheaper mini WiFi cameras or IP cameras:\n\n- Only work on the same local WiFi network.\n- Do not support remote viewing unless you set up port forwarding or a VPN.\n- May require technical setup.\n\n👉 In this case, you **must be on the same network** unless you configure remote access manually.\n\n---\n\n### 🔎 Quick Rule\n- If the camera uses a mobile app with login → works anywhere with internet.\n- If it only shows up via IP address (like 192.168.x.x) → same network only.\n\n---\n\nIf you tell me the brand or model, I can explain exactly how that one works."
          ]
        },
